# Code guideline modules (index)

These **`.mdc`** files govern **architectural patterns** for DriveStream Next.js BFF portals. They live in the **`nextjs-bff-rules`** repository and are consumed via a **git submodule** at each portal repo's **`.cursor/rules/`** (this directory when mounted).

**Product-specific** requirements, upstream service maps, route catalogs, ADRs, and feature trackers belong in each portal repo under **`docs/specification/`**, **`docs/project-guidance/`**, and **README** — not in this package.

## Process rules (this package)

| File | Topic |
|------|--------|
| **`spec-driven-development.mdc`** | SDD truth hierarchy, same-PR discipline, PR traceability |
| **`testing-verify-flows.mdc`** | Vitest unit vs live verify; feature map; no-overlap policy |

## Stack and BFF rules (this package)

| File | Topic |
|------|--------|
| **`nextjs-app-router-stack.mdc`** | Next.js App Router, React, TypeScript, Tailwind, TanStack Query |
| **`nextjs-bff-server-auth.mdc`** | httpOnly session, `authFetch`, server-only upstream |
| **`nextjs-bff-route-handlers.mdc`** | `app/api/**/route.ts` — logging, errors, upstream fetch |
| **`nextjs-repository-layout.mdc`** | `app/`, `components/`, `lib/`; BFF by upstream service |
| **`typescript-react-style.mdc`** | Strict TS, functional components, hooks |
| **`client-forms-patterns.mdc`** | Client forms, TanStack Query mutations |
| **`tailwind-design-tokens.mdc`** | CSS variables, `components/ui` primitives |
| **`shared-limits-pagination.mdc`** | Pagination and limits via `@/lib/constants` |
| **`no-hardcoded-strings.mdc`** | i18n — `data/locales/en/` |
| **`workspace-page-layout.mdc`** | `WorkspacePage` / header shell |
| **`documentation-project-guidance.mdc`** | `docs/project-guidance/` vs `docs/specification/` |

## Per-repository product documentation

Each portal repo should provide (not in this package):

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **`docs/specification/product/`** | Capabilities, `02-route-map.md`, initiative specs |
| **`docs/specification/adr/`** | Architecture decision records |
| **`docs/specification/as-built/`** | Live vs deferred; verification matrix |
| **`docs/project-guidance/`** | Portal UX, CRUD patterns, branding |
| **`AGENTS.md`** | Agent router — rules boundary, verify commands |
| **`tests/README.md`** | Unit vs verify feature map |
| **`README.md`** | Setup, env vars, pinned **`nextjs-bff-rules`** version |

## Cross-project conventions

- **Do not** add upstream service names (Abhilekh, Parichay, …) to shared **`.mdc`** files — use **`product/00-service-profile.md`** and **`product/02-route-map.md`** in the consumer repo.
- **Do not** edit **`.cursor/rules/`** in consumer repos — propose changes via PR on [nextjs-bff-rules](https://github.com/drivestream-lab/nextjs-bff-rules).
- **Harness:** consumer pin in **`.harness-pin.yaml`** (`profile: frontend`); from tenant meta run `launchpad sync-harness-app --repo <portal-repo> --apply` (see [harness pins](https://github.com/drivestream-lab/launchpad/blob/main/playbook/harness-pins.md)).
